# The rows of src/runtime/Ports.h and src/runtime/Ports.cpp, a call each (src/tools/bench/bench.py).

## Ports.cpp/axes, window lines and sound, with no window
a frame of 4: 4 frames
input axis gamepad_a 0 0 -> refused: gamepad_a is no axis: an axis is gamepad_left or gamepad_right, a stick, or gamepad_left_trigger or gamepad_right_trigger
input axis gamepad_left 0.5 -1 -> 
input axis gamepad_left 1.5 0 -> refused: gamepad_left 1.5 0: a stick's x and y go from -1 to 1, a trigger's x from 0 to 1, its y 0
input axis gamepad_left nan 0 -> refused: nan is not a finite number
input axis gamepad_left_trigger 0.5 0.5 -> refused: gamepad_left_trigger 0.5 0.5: a stick's x and y go from -1 to 1, a trigger's x from 0 to 1, its y 0
input axis gamepad_right_trigger -0.1 0 -> refused: gamepad_right_trigger -0.1 0: a stick's x and y go from -1 to 1, a trigger's x from 0 to 1, its y 0
input axis gamepad_right_trigger 1 0 -> 
played, after the next frame started: 0.5 -0.25 1 -1 0 0 0.5 0.5; it holds 2 frames
the frame after: game's a reads [axis "gamepad_left" (0.5,-1), axis "gamepad_right_trigger" (1,0)]
window fullscreen off -> refused: unknown command window fullscreen off; the commands window starts are window pointer free, window pointer lock, window title <value>...
window fullscreen on -> refused: unknown command window fullscreen on; the commands window starts are window pointer free, window pointer lock, window title <value>...
window pointer free -> freed the pointer; no window is open, so it waits for one
window pointer lock -> locked the pointer in the window; no window is open, so it waits for one
window title a  named window -> named the window a named window; no window is open, so it waits for one

